    {
      "role": "step",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eCompare the two decimals.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eChecking from the left, the first place where they differ is the hundredths place. Here, the first value has a 3, whereas the second value has an 8.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eSo, the second value is greater. Use a less than sign.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003cimg width\u003d\"80\" height\u003d\"41\" src\u003d\"/modules/gcprealgpractice/gcprealgpractice_8_1_realnumbersandthepythagoreantheorem_7_70/image035.gif\" class\u003d\"middle\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
